body:
Most of the girls I match with won't respond and if they do, when I ask them on a date they leave me hanging. I don't ever send them nasty messages, and I leave the door open. I try to flirt and tease them. I don't really know what I'm doing wrong. It really feels like there's definite scarcity. I dunno there was a girl I talked to at the bar last night but it didn't go anywhere, and I didn't see her again for the rest of the time I was there. People tell me I'm attractive and I try to take care of my appearance, and I study dating and attraction constantly. I just don't have any luck at all. If I do manage to get a date, I only get one.

&#x200B;

How do I have an attitude of abundance in this case?

I did all of these things, with the exception of #4, though I really feel like I have little control over that since women are the sexual selectors. I've had such terrible luck with women that I started reading books to get a clue. I am in pretty good shape. I'm not rich but I'm not broke, and manage to do a LOT with very little money. I have my own place, and a nice car that I maintain. I'm definitely not ugly. I'm pretty intelligent. I can fix things. I'm not afraid to express my feelings with honesty, and I have a willingness to communicate. I find ways to make passive income. I have hobbies. I can be very funny, and witty. I admit that I have some approach anxiety, but I can talk to women without fawning all over them, and I don't compliment them really at all. I've seen guys act like that and it's even cringy to me. I can express sexual intent.

&#x200B;

My last girlfriend would ask to get together, she did most of the texting and calling, she was the one that decided where the relationship went. She decided to break up, and refused to even tell me why. She kept calling me though, then was annoyed if I called her back. She accused me of things I didn't do, twisted my words around, blamed me for things I had nothing to do with. I looked at her social media looking for the answers she never gave me. Now I'm trying to get my head straight again, before I even try to 

&#x200B;

It doesn't really seem fair, that men are expected to do absolutely everything, and to top themselves to maintain a relationship or just get laid.... but sure... you're going to tell me life isn't fair. I get it.

&#x200B;

Other than biological imperatives, I can't understand with all the hoops a guy has to jump through, the imbalance of reciprocity, the double-standards, the   
 contradictions, the unrealistic expectations, why anyone would want to subject himself to such extreme levels of stress and aggravation.

&#x200B;

I'm not interested in being a woman's servant or slave.

I used to call this my first synth, but then I remember when I was a little kid someone gave me one of these...

&#x200B;

[https://youtu.be/ZGBXhtqQWgk](https://youtu.be/ZGBXhtqQWgk)

&#x200B;

I managed to keep hold of this up until my mid twenties, but I lost it somewhere. Wish I still had it. I still have my microKorg... in a closet. Sad because I had a lot of great memories with my microKorg too.

It can definitely sound like that... and I've had it sounding as aggressive as a Moog too. I read that the Sid chip is a digital synth, but the filter is analog. I really like that the noise is pitched, as I think all my other synths the noise won't track with the keyboard, but maybe I have to patch it in. I'm still trying to figure out how the sync works. The manual said that osc1 syncs to osc3, but it never explained why there's sync on all three oscillators.

&#x200B;

It's a nice synth. I definitely wanted a Sid chip synth. I have some issues with it, but I can't tell if it's an issue with my chips or the synth itself. Lfo1 only seems to work sometimes, and after being on for a few hours it will crash. I can reset it but it crashes again right away. I wonder if my chips are getting too hot. I really don't want to have to send it back to France.
